Tender bone-in pork chops slow-cooked all day in a rich cream of mushroom and chicken gravy with sliced onions and fresh mushrooms.

*Adapted from [Spend With Pennies](https://www.spendwithpennies.com/crock-pot-pork-chops/#wprm-recipe-container-134606).*

## Ingredients

- 4 bone-in pork chops (about 3 pounds)
- Salt and black pepper, to taste
- ½ teaspoon paprika
- ½ teaspoon garlic powder
- 1 tablespoon olive oil
- 1 can (10.5 oz) condensed cream of mushroom soup
- 1 can (10.5 oz) condensed cream of chicken soup
- ¾ cup reduced-sodium beef broth
- 2 cups sliced mushrooms
- 1 small onion, sliced

## Instructions

1. **Brown the Chops:** Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Season pork chops generously on both sides with salt, pepper, paprika, and garlic powder. Sear for about 3 minutes per side until nicely browned.
2. **Deglaze the Pan:** Remove pork chops from the skillet. Pour in the cream of mushroom soup, cream of chicken soup, and beef broth. Whisk well to scrape up all the flavorful browned bits from the pan.
3. **Layer the Slow Cooker:** Scatter the sliced mushrooms and onions evenly across the bottom of the slow cooker. Lay the browned pork chops on top, then pour the warm soup mixture over everything.
4. **Slow Cook:** Cover and cook on LOW for 7 to 8 hours until the pork is fork-tender.
5. **Serve:** Serve warm with gravy ladled over mashed potatoes, steamed rice, or egg noodles.

## Notes

- **Thickening Slurry:** If you prefer an extra thick gravy, whisk together 2 tablespoons cornstarch with 2 tablespoons cold water. Stir into the slow cooker 20–30 minutes before serving and cook on HIGH until thickened.
- **Pork Chops:** Bone-in pork chops hold up best to long slow cooking without drying out. Thick-cut chops are recommended.
